Subject: vms/config_h.com: comment out #if blocks whose condition is continued

gawk 5.4.1's configh.in has autoconf's C23 bool check, an #if whose
condition spans several lines.  config_h.com passed the first line through
and commented out the continuation lines, leaving an unterminated #if, so
every compilation failed with %CC-E-NORIGHTPAREN at config.h line 783.
Comment out such a block up to its #endif; for DEC C it is a no-op, since
HAVE_C_BOOL is defined.

--- a/vms/config_h.com	2026-10-03 20:41:59.890224515 +0100
+++ b/vms/config_h.com	2026-10-03 20:41:59.909619648 +0100
@@ -292,6 +292,18 @@
 $   endif
 $!
 $!
+$!  An #if whose condition continues on the next lines (ends in "\"),
+$!  such as autoconf's C23 bool check, cannot be passed through line by
+$!  line: comment out the whole block up to its #endif.  For DEC C the
+$!  block is a no-op anyway, as HAVE_C_BOOL is defined below.
+$!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
+$   if keyif .eqs. "#if" .and. f$extract(xlen - 1, 1, xline) .eqs. "\"
+$   then
+$	write tf "/* ", xline, " */"
+$	if_block = 3
+$	goto cfgh_in_loop1
+$   endif
+$!
 $!  Default action for an #if/#else/#endif
 $!------------------------------------------
 $   if keyif .eqs. "#if" .or. keyif .eqs. "#el"
